# Audit evidence is committed BY ITS HASH.  Every artifact here is listed in a
# MANIFEST.sha256 that a reader is expected to verify with `sha256sum -c`.
#
# The captures were taken on Windows and carry CRLF in the blob.  Without these
# rules, a clone with `core.autocrlf=true` (which is the SYSTEM setting on the
# owner's desktop) would convert them on checkout, the materialized bytes would
# stop matching the manifest, and a perfectly honest clone would report the
# evidence as corrupt.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion: the bytes on disk are the bytes
# in the blob, in every clone, under every configuration.  That is the only
# thing that makes a hash-verified artifact portable, and this lane learned it
# the expensive way -- see Addendum 581 on the materialization identity.
#
# Patterns without a slash match at any depth, so future evidence directories
# are covered without editing this file.

*.log            -text
*.txt            -text
*.lean           -text
*.sh             -text
MANIFEST.sha256  -text
